<h1>Getting Started</h1>

<h2>Install the extension</h2>

<p>From the project root, in order:</p>

<ol>
  <li>Install dependencies once: <code>npm install</code></li>
  <li>Build the bundle: <code>npm run build</code></li>
  <li>Package it: <code>npx @vscode/vsce package</code></li>
  <li>Install into your main VS Code: <code>code --install-extension hd-editor-0.1.0.vsix --force</code></li>
  <li>Reload VS Code: <strong>Ctrl+Shift+P</strong> → "Developer: Reload Window".</li>
</ol>

<p>For ongoing iteration the build / package / install steps can be chained:</p>

<pre><code>npm run build; npx @vscode/vsce package; code --install-extension hd-editor-0.1.0.vsix --force</code></pre>

<h2>Create your first .hd file</h2>

<p>Create any file with a <code>.hd</code> extension in a workspace. VS Code launches the HD WYSIWYG editor as the default editor for that file. On first open, the editor injects an <code>id</code> and a <code>version</code> into the frontmatter — you don't need to set them by hand.</p>

<p>If you want to seed your own frontmatter, start the file with a bare YAML fence:</p>

<pre><code>---
title: My Document
description: A short description.
---

&lt;h1&gt;Hello, HD&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;…&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre>

<h2>Editor basics</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Toolbar</strong> at the top: headings, bold/italic/underline, inline code, code block, links, lists, blockquote, horizontal rule, insert table.</li>
  <li><strong>Tables</strong>: hover near the top to insert columns, near the left to insert rows. Right-click any cell for the full menu (delete column/row, toggle headers, delete table). Hover a column boundary to resize.</li>
  <li><strong>Paste from Markdown</strong>: paste Markdown text — the editor detects it and converts automatically.</li>
  <li><strong>Paste from HTML</strong>: paste HTML from Notion, Linear, or browsers — the editor sanitizes against the HD allow-list.</li>
  <li><strong>Copy as Markdown</strong>: <strong>Ctrl+Shift+P</strong> → "HD: Copy as Markdown".</li>
</ul>

